  "type": "Key Takeaway",
  "number": "1.2.5",
  "title": "Three Ways to Describe a Set.",
  "body": " Three Ways to Describe a Set  A set can be described in three ways.  In words: is the set of odd numbers between and .  By listing (the roster method): .  In set-builder notation : , read the set of all such that is an odd number and is between and .    Dots show a pattern: goes on for ever, while stops at . Some books write a vertical bar instead of the colon: .  "
