  "body": " Rules on the Road   Work with a partner.   A speed-limit sign and the speeds it allows.   A round speed-limit sign showing 50 beside a number line from 40 to 60 with a filled circle at 50 and a thick line to the left.        A sign in Nakuru town shows a speed limit of . Write the rule for a driver's speed, .  .    You must be at least years old to vote. Write the rule for a voter's age, years.  .    Milk in a dairy fridge must be kept below . Write the rule for the temperature, .  .    More than fans watched a match at Kasarani. Write this for the number of fans, .  .    Draw each rule on a number line.  Filled circles at and at , because these values are allowed; open circles at and at , because they are not. The thick line goes left from and from , and right from and from .    Which of the speeds , and obey rule (a)?  and . A driver at exactly is within the limit; is over it.    Discuss with your partner: why do rules (a) and (c) use different signs?  The speed limit allows itself ( at most ), so the sign is . Below does not allow itself, so the sign is .      "
