  "title": "A Coin and a Die Together.",
  "body": " A Coin and a Die Together   Toss a coin and roll a die at the same time.     List all the possible outcomes, such as H1 (head and 1). How many are there?  H1, H2, H3, H4, H5, H6, T1, T2, T3, T4, T5, T6: outcomes, .    Find the probability of a head and a 6.  One outcome, H6: .    Find the probability of a tail and an even number.  T2, T4, T6: .    Now roll two dice and add the scores. Draw a grid of all the totals. How many outcomes are there?  A grid: outcomes (see ).    Otieno says: There are 11 possible totals, from 2 to 12, so the probability of a total of 7 is . Is he right?  No. The totals are not equally likely: six of the cells have total 7, so , while only one cell has total 2.      "
