  "number": "10.2.24",
  "title": "Structured Instruction.",
  "body": " Structured Instruction    Suggested Time 8 minutes  Objective To define a discrete random variable and its probability distribution.     Key Takeaways & Teacher Connection   Connecting to Learner Work: the table in part (b) is a probability distribution.  Capital names the random variable; small is one of its values.  Two checks: every probability is from 0 to 1; the probabilities add to 1.  Add rows for at least , and remember that at least 2 includes 2.    "
